yndrome: typically presents with cytopenias but not such high blast counts in peripheral blood", "Autoimmune pancytopenia: would require additional lab evidence (e.g., reticulocytosis, autoantibodies)"], "alarm_features": ["Constitutional B symptoms (fever, night sweats, weight loss)", "Visual acuity decline in a thin, malnourished patient"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.15943822161022364, "posterior": 0.01453854080027905, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["Absence of lymphoid markers directly rules out lymphoid neoplasms (B2) and plasma cell disorders (B3) as explanations for the blast count."], "evidence_against": ["35% blasts in peripheral blood are pathognomonic for CML in blast crisis (B4) rather than chronic phase CML, which typically has <5% blasts."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.8, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["acute myeloid leukemia", "myelodysplastic syndrome with excess blasts", "chronic myeloid leukemia in blast crisis"]}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.16716999495552817, "posterior": 0.037877139072782604, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["Absence of lymphoid markers directly rules out lymphoid neoplasms (B2) and plasma cell disorders (B3) as explanations for the blast count."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.7, "interrupt_relevance": 0.8, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representat